<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Fredericton</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Fredericton is the capital of the Canadian province of New <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/brunswick">Brunswick</a>, on the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/saint-john-river">Saint John River</a>. Founded by Loyalists in 1785 near the former Acadian settlement of Sainte-Anne's Point, it was chosen as capital by Governor <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/thomas-carleton">Thomas Carleton</a> because it was safer from attack than the port of Saint John. It is home to the University of New Brunswick, founded in 1785.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/fredericton.jpg" alt="Fredericton" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Quintin Soloviev · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Fredericton,_New_Brunswick_aerial_view_(cropped).jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
